To develop the Project we need to follow the SDLC
      i.e , Planning, Requirement Analysis, Design, Implement, Test, Deploy,
Maintain.

Here we two models:
1. waterfall model: A linear and sequential approach, where each Phase must
be completed before the next begins.
>Code Everything, Test and Deploy

2. agile model: 
>Code, Test and Deploy Every 2 weeks
        here we also as the DevOps model comes under the agile

3. devops model:
>Code, Test, Deploy Continuously

DevOps Life Cycle:
Developers:
1.continuous development: Plan, code
2. continuous testing: build, test

          (continuous integration)
Operations:
3. continuous deployment: release, deploy
4. continuous monitoring: operte, monitor


>Client Server Architecture
Client:which request the resource(resource like imformation) is the client
ex:Browser
Server:which respond to the resource
note: the client and server should be in the same Network if they need
to comunicate to each other
> In the Network all are called as devices and here the devices can be
either Client or Server
>devices in network use IP or host name for comunication (hostname:name of the server)

Note:static website as no database where as the dynamic will have database

>Types of Architecture:
1. 1-Tier Architecture:
* If the website is running in the localhost or localmachine is called
1-Tier Architecture 
*like it as only one layer in that only both the client and server in same
machine

2. 2-Tier Architecture:
*In this layer we have seperate the client and the server seperately

3. 3-Tier Architecture: or N-Tier
* In this layer we have seperate the client, server layer (application layer, and database layer)

Client-->webserver-->application server-->Database Layer

>application server: the server where the application hosted is called Application server
>Database server: the server which as database installed or data stored is the database server
>web server: which takes the request from clients and redirect to application server
Note: we have different environment:
client->Production environment->pre-production environment->test environment->Dev Environment->developer
(<--)
>actually the application and the database server is in the private network
so now to access this we need the webserver between client and application











        
